B.afg=new A.bi("Under this section, the learner is expected to have a better understanding of all the dashboard lights and warnings and what they meaning.\n\nCommon lights & warnings you should know may include;\n\nCheck engine warning, battery warning, coolant temperature light, transmission temperature, oil pressure warning, tire pressure monitoring system, brake system, airbag warning, lamp out, washer fluid, door open, low fuel, headlights, seatbelt indicator, front fog lights, high-beam indicator, automatic high-beam indicator, automatic emergency braking.",null,B.H,B.b9)
B.afh=new A.bi("There are three (3) main categories of road signs namely;",null,B.H,B.b_)
B.afi=new A.bi("\nThese are also known as prohibitory or regulatory signs. \n\n These are signs which are obligatory on the traffic which uses a specific area of road. \n\nThese signs indicate what must one do, rather than must not do. \n\nMandatory Road signs are generally round in shape with red border. \n\nExamples of regulatory signs include stop, yield, do not enter, no turn on left, no turn on right, no parking, weight limit, speed limit, one way and HOV lane ahead. \n\nThey are used to regulate the flow of traffic, regulatory signs are arguably the most important type of traffic signs.\n\nViolation of these signs attracts heavy fines and punishments.",null,B.H,B.aI)
B.afH=new A.A(!0,B.b,null,null,null,null,10,B.v,B.a7,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
B.afj=new A.bi("(C P S \u2013 A KEY TO KNOW ALL ROAD SIGNS)",null,B.H,B.afH)
B.afk=new A.bi("\nSuch licenses are often plastic and the size of a credit card as shown in the image above",null,B.H,B.d6)
B.afl=new A.bi("\nThis section describes the testing procedures for one to acquire a driving license. \n\nThe IOV (Inspectorate of Vehicles) test consists of both theory and practical.\n\nThe pass mark for the overall test is 75%",null,B.H,B.d6)
B.afm=new A.bi("This consists of steering wheel and  steering wheel mechanism.\n\nIt is responsible for directing the car where to go.",null,B.H,B.b9)
B.afn=new A.bi("\nThese are also known as caution or hazard signs. \n\nWarning signs let you know that road changes are coming up on your drive. \nThese can be permanent or temporary traffic hazards and obstacles.",null,B.H,B.aI)
B.afo=new A.bi("This is considered the heart and lungs of a vehicle.\n\nIt consists of the engine, transmission, driveshaft. The engine helps in the burning of fuel into mechanical energy which moves the vehicle.",null,B.H,B.b9)
B.afp=new A.bi("\nIt is a simplified representation used to explain the types of roads found in major towns of Uganda and East Africa.\n\nIt is a driving simulator or model road board used for teaching and practicing road skills, especially in a driving school setting.",null,B.H,B.aI)
B.afq=new A.bi("Road signs can be interpreted by use of;",null,B.H,B.ah)
B.afr=new A.bi("\nIn Uganda, a learner should be above 18 years is required to have a Learner Driving Licence (LDL) and undertake instructions from a licenced instructor. From here, a learner can obtain his or her driving licence after being assessed by the IOV ",null,B.H,B.aI)
B.afs=new A.bi("This consists of brake pedal, brake fluids, wheels.\n\nIt ensures the vehicle can stop safely when required.",null,B.H,B.b9)
B.aft=new A.bi("Traffic or vehicles are required to stop and look right, left and right again and only proceed if the road is clear.",null,B.H,B.aI)
B.afu=new A.bi("b) Flush / parallel / uncontrolled parking. \n\nThis type of parking is found on the left side of the road in the direction of traffic.\n\nHas no security thus it is uncontrolled parking zone.",null,B.H,B.aI)
B.afv=new A.bi("This shape represents warning or cautionary or alerting signs.",null,B.H,B.ah)
B.afw=new A.bi("\nA driver`s license is a legal authorization, or the official document confirming such an authorization, for a specific individual to operate one or more types of motorized vehicles\u2014such as motorcycles, cars, trucks, or buses\u2014on a public road",null,B.H,B.d6)
B.afx=new A.bi("\nIt is marked in a yellow painted line.\n\na) A yellow continuous dividing line. \n\n --> means no overtaking or changing lanes on both sides.\n\nb) A yellow dotted / broken line \n\n --> means you may overtake if it the road is clear.",null,B.H,B.aI)
